{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/275174-a-freshly-risen-monster","id":275174,"title":"A Freshly Risen Monster","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-07T20:38:53-07:00","id":275174,"title":"A Freshly Risen Monster","content":"Why is a mummy that you have just awoken particularly terrible? Does Sekhem 10 really impart that much of a tangible advantage? Help me understand why a just-woken mummy is so scary...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T20:51:44-07:00","id":275191,"title":"","content":"A Sekhem 10 Mummy who picks Physical Attributes as their Tertiary option and gives themselves 2 Strength, 2 Dexterity, and 2 Stamina can, in a single turn, reflexively rise to Strength 10, Dexterity 8, Stamina 10 by spending 5 Pillars. And then hit someone that same turn. Even without any Brawl or Weaponry at all, that's still 9 dice from an entirely unskilled combatant.<br /> <br /> Now take into account thousands of years in which to learn at least the basics of some kind of fighting skill and... well, it doesn't take a lot before the dice pools start getting silly.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, certain Utterances are stronger the higher your Sekhem (Secrets Ripped From Skies calls down meteor strikes that automatically set the target on fire and do Sheut + Occult + Sekhem as the attack roll), and it means that a Mummy is almost impossible to put down. When a Mummy first rises, it's Sekhem 10 and Memory 0. When a Sekhem 10 Memory 0 Mummy dies, it returns to life within seconds. It spends only as long in its Death Cycle as it takes for the enemy to drop their guard, and then it gets a free surprise attack with the aforementioned Strength 10 (well, probably 8 or 9, since the Sekhem would likely drop from the Death Cycle, but still high).<br /> <br /> A few Affinities make this even worse. Wisdom of the Ancients, if I remember right, lets you boost you Mental Attributes as well as your Physical ones. Two more pillar points and you could be looking at a Defence 8+ Mummy.<br /> <br /> Coupled with the natural Mummy advantages, like being able to Seal the Flesh, they're a pretty terrifying prospect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 10-08-2014, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T02:38:52-07:00","id":275285,"title":"","content":"Note: Azahul mentioned both the fact that the mummy is level 10 in power, another scary part is their &quot;integrity&quot; stat is 0. Unless you know how to immediately remind a mummy via flashback or convincing iremite, it may just kill you for being there. They suffer no &quot;breaking points&quot; for their first scene of activity. To illustrate, one of my pcs plays a young high priest wooing a mummy that isnt his master. When the lover Mummy was resurrected, he almost killed his lover because he didnt know any call phrases, secret handshakes, or anything that told the angry mummy &quot;dont kill me, im a friend&quot;. Slinging around those dicepools with no idea who anyone is can be devastating. If your high priest stumbles in his prayers.. Despite knowing your for thirty years, you could snap his neck because of his error in one round with your boosted attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T17:42:51-07:00","id":275899,"title":"","content":"It's really a combination of high power and few qualms. As the book says, &quot;The Arisen might be confused and bleary in terms of memory, but he\u2019s absolutely clear-thinking in terms of action and decision-making . . . In fact, thanks to the near-overload of Sekhem upon first arising, a newly awakened mummy is far more likely to resort to violence\u2014regardless of his normal personality\u2014than at almost any other time in his waking life. The urge to burn off some of that power, coming as it does during the period of activity in which the Arisen feels the least connection or kinship to mortal beings, makes the spending of Sekhem (whether on physical augmentation or sorcery) almost instinctive.&quot; So basically the Mummy is fully capable of taking any appropriate action to defend himself or his tomb, or even acting dangerously in a state of divine confusion if appropriately summoned by means of a cult Call. He is even more likely to do so, given Memory 0 - he may not necessarily intend to do something that might appear sociopathic, but do it anyway. For example, in an attempt to be showy in front of his cult, he might unloose Revelations of Smoke and Flame Tier 3, unaware that he's not in his normal tomb, but in a place full of flammable materials.<br /> <br /> And also the increase of clarity that comes even at Sekhem 9 (usually when Memory has reasserted itself) means he might not resort to violence as immediately at that level, though he is certainly just as capable as Sekhem 9 as at Sekhem 10.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}